{"title":"Career Roadmap: Pastry Chef","role":"Pastry Chef","summary":"A Pastry Chef specializes in the production and presentation of:","facts":{"Current degree":"Hospitality, Travel & Aviation","Course":"BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Develop professional pastry, bakery, chocolate, confectionery, food-safety, kitchen-management and hospitality skills for a career in professional pastry kitchens"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Pastry Chef specializes in the production and presentation of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Breads"},{"text":"Cakes"},{"text":"Pastries"},{"text":"Tarts"},{"text":"Cookies"},{"text":"Desserts"},{"text":"Chocolates"},{"text":"Confectionery"},{"text":"Frozen desserts"},{"text":"Plated desserts"},{"text":"Viennoiserie"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The career combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Culinary Technique","Food Science","Creativity","Kitchen Operations","Cost Control","Hospitality"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"A hospitality degree provides a broad foundation, but becoming a strong Pastry Chef requires substantial practical kitchen training and progressive professional experience. A graduate normally begins as a Commis/Commis Pastry or Junior Pastry Cook before progressing to higher chef positions."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Culinary & food foundations"},{"text":"Food science, hygiene, kitchen operations"},{"text":"Basic pastry portfolio"},{"text":"Weak fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Pastry & bakery techniques"},{"text":"Baking, confectionery, chocolate, breads"},{"text":"15–20 documented products"},{"text":"Inconsistent execution"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Advanced pa